Python exception When <code>ConfigError</code> The target is unknown or ambiguous, <code>environment</code> is invalid, or <code>ESAF_FOLDER</code> isn't set. <code>BlockedError</code> The server's review refused the call, or another job is still running on the Factory. <code>AuthError</code> The API key is missing or wrong, or the API isn't on the same machine. <code>FailureError</code> The API failed, or its storage is unavailable. <pre><code>from azurefactory import esaf
from azurefactory.errors import BlockedError, ConfigError

try:
    job = esaf.delete_project("002", "dev", wait=True)
except BlockedError as error:
    print("Refused:", error.message, error.details.get("blockers"))
except ConfigError as error:
    print("Check the call:", error.message)
</code></pre> <p>Next: Quickstart: Create your AI Factory</p> <p>Related: ESAF usage guide · Guide 17: deletion prerequisites · Maintainers: the step-by-step review flow</p>
